                <pb facs="0651" n="642" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg642"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6251: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Leopoldville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mallon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-30T11:00:00-05:00">October 30,
                            1940—11 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Consulate at Dakar reports that fighting has taken place in Gabon and that
                    airplanes and infantry officers have been sent there as reinforcements. Please
                    comment briefly by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
